omxplorer, a desktop spreadsheet app for data scientists (1440x900), showing sales-1m (1,000,000 rows). Top: a slim floating menu bar (File, Edit, View, Insert, Data, Format, Help) with the Format menu open as a panel: Bold Ctrl+B, Italic Ctrl+I, Underline Ctrl+U, Strikethrough Ctrl+5, a divider, Text colour ›, Fill colour ›, Align ›, a divider, Format as ›, Clear formatting, a divider, Format inspector (checked). Below it one floating toolbar island of icon-above-label buttons: [Save, Undo] [Add row, Formula, Sort, Pivot, Chart] [Bold, Italic, Underline, Strikethrough, Text colour, Fill, Align left/centre/right, Currency] [Format]. A formula bar: cell reference "B4", "fx", the value "4612.00". The grid fills the window: row-number gutter, columns order (#), amount (0.0), region (Aa), day (date), paid (bool), each header with a type badge and a tiny histogram; realistic rows (amounts like 8922.63, regions South/North/East/West/Central, days like 2025-03-03, paid true/false), some empty amount cells. A block of cells B3:C8 is selected (a range: teal ring, soft fill, a fill handle). Right: a floating inspector panel 300px with a segmented control "Format · Column · Table", showing NUMBER (Auto / Number / Currency / Percent), decimals stepper, thousands separator switch, then COLUMN STATS for amount with a histogram. Bottom strip: sheet tabs "Sheet" (active) "Report" "+", and selection figures "Sum 31,842.07 · Average 5,307.01 · Count 6 · RTX 4090 · 0.3 ms".
